Task Contract","title":"Ensamblador de contexto CCDD Nivel 2"}},{"id":"contracts/assemble-context.md#88","metadata":{"content":"por stdout).","okf_concept":"contracts/assemble-context.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Ensamblador de contexto CCDD Nivel 2"}},{"id":"contracts/assemble-context.md#89","metadata":{"content":"por stdout).","okf_concept":"contracts/assemble-context.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Ensamblador de contexto CCDD Nivel 2"}},{"id":"contracts/assemble-context.md#9","metadata":{"content":"ato\ninválido o guardrail abort · 1 I/O.","okf_concept":"contracts/assemble-context.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Ensamblador de contexto CCDD Nivel 2"}},{"id":"contracts/assemble-context.md#90","metadata":{"content":"or stdout).","okf_concept":"contracts/assemble-context.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Ensamblador de contexto CCDD Nivel 2"}},{"id":"contracts/assemble-context.md#91","metadata":{"content":"r stdout).","okf_concept":"contracts/assemble-context.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Ensamblador de contexto CCDD Nivel 2"}},{"id":"contracts/assemble-context.md#92","metadata":{"content":"stdout).","okf_concept":"contracts/assemble-context.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Ensamblador de contexto CCDD Nivel 2"}},{"id":"contracts/assemble-context.md#93","metadata":{"content":"stdout).","okf_concept":"contracts/assemble-context.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Ensamblador de contexto CCDD Nivel 2"}},{"id":"contracts/assemble-context.md#94","metadata":{"content":"tdout).","okf_concept":"contracts/assemble-context.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Ensamblador de contexto CCDD Nivel 2"}},{"id":"contracts/assemble-context.md#95","metadata":{"content":"dout).","okf_concept":"contracts/assemble-context.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Ensamblador de contexto CCDD Nivel 2"}},{"id":"contracts/assemble-context.md#96","metadata":{"content":"out).","okf_concept":"contracts/assemble-context.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Ensamblador de contexto CCDD Nivel 2"}},{"id":"contracts/assemble-context.md#97","metadata":{"content":"ut).","okf_concept":"contracts/assemble-context.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Ensamblador de contexto CCDD Nivel 2"}},{"id":"contracts/assemble-context.md#98","metadata":{"content":"t).","okf_concept":"contracts/assemble-context.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Ensamblador de contexto CCDD Nivel 2"}},{"id":"contracts/assemble-context.md#99","metadata":{"content":").","okf_concept":"contracts/assemble-context.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Ensamblador de contexto CCDD Nivel 2"}},{"id":"contracts/attestation-gate.md#0","metadata":{"content":"# Contract: Gate de atestacion (validate_attestation)","okf_concept":"contracts/attestation-gate.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Gate de atestacion de reportes locales (.agents/logs, Nivel local)"}},{"id":"contracts/attestation-gate.md#1","metadata":{"content":"tract: Gate de atestacion (validate_attestation)","okf_concept":"contracts/attestation-gate.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Gate de atestacion de reportes locales (.agents/logs, Nivel local)"}},{"id":"contracts/attestation-gate.md#10","metadata":{"content":"te de atestacion (validate_attestation)","okf_concept":"contracts/attestation-gate.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Gate de atestacion de reportes locales (.agents/logs, Nivel local)"}},{"id":"contracts/attestation-gate.md#100","metadata":{"content":"## Interface\n- `REQUIRED_KEYS` — tupla de las 9 claves obligatorias del envelope:\n  `task`, `agent`, `model`, `command`, `exit_code`, `output_sha256`,\n  `contract_sha256`, `repo_head`, `timestamp`.\n- `parse_envelope(text) -> (dict|None, str)` — dict de\n  `{clave: valor_string}` del bloque YAML entre los primeros dos\n  delimitadores `---`, y el `body` (todo lo que sigue). `(None, text)` si\n  no hay envelope valido.\n- `validate_report(path, repo_root) -> [{'file','level','rule','msg'}]` —\n  valida un unico REPORT.","okf_concept":"contracts/attestation-gate.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Gate de atestacion de reportes locales (.agents/logs, Nivel local)"}},{"id":"contracts/attestation-gate.md#101","metadata":{"content":"el','rule','msg'}]` —\n  valida un unico REPORT. Reglas: `ENVELOPE_MISSING` (WARNING, unico\n  finding si aplica), `MISSING_KEY` (ERROR, una por clave ausente/vacia),\n  `TASK_MISMATCH` (ERROR, `task` no coincide con el nombre de archivo),\n  `EXIT_CODE_INVALID`/`EXIT_CODE_NONZERO` (ERROR), `OUTPUT_HASH_MISMATCH`\n  (ERROR), `CONTRACT_MISSING`/`CONTRACT_HASH_MISMATCH` (ERROR). Cada\n  chequeo posterior a `ENVELOPE_MISSING` solo corre si sus claves\n  relevantes estan presentes (evita cascadas de findings espurios desde\n  una sola clave faltante).\n- `validate_directory(logs_dir, repo_root='.') -> [findings]` — valida\n  cada `*-REPORT.md` de `logs_dir` (no recursivo), excluye\n  `TEMPLATE-REPORT.md`.","okf_concept":"contracts/attestation-gate.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Gate de atestacion de reportes locales (.agents/logs, Nivel local)"}},{"id":"contracts/attestation-gate.md#102","metadata":{"content":"` (no recursivo), excluye\n  `TEMPLATE-REPORT.md`. Directorio inexistente -> `[]` (sin `.agents/logs/`\n  local, nada que auditar, no es error).\n- `main(argv) -> int` — `argv[1]`=logs_dir (default `.agents/logs`),\n  `argv[2]`=repo_root (default `.`). Exit 0 si no hay ningun finding\n  ERROR (los WARNING como `ENVELOPE_MISSING` NO bloquean —\n  retrocompatibilidad con reportes escritos antes de este gate); 1 si\n  hay >=1 ERROR.","okf_concept":"contracts/attestation-gate.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Gate de atestacion de reportes locales (.agents/logs, Nivel local)"}},{"id":"contracts/attestation-gate.md#103","metadata":{"content":"ritos antes de este gate); 1 si\n  hay >=1 ERROR.\n\n## Invariants\n- `parse_envelope` nunca lanza excepcion sobre texto arbitrario (sin\n  envelope -> `(None, text)` completo, nunca crashea).\n- `validate_report` sobre un REPORT sin envelope devuelve EXACTAMENTE un\n  finding (`ENVELOPE_MISSING`, WARNING) — ningun otro chequeo corre.\n- `validate_directory` sobre un directorio inexistente devuelve `[]`, no\n  levanta `OSError`.\n- `TEMPLATE-REPORT.md` siempre se excluye, sin importar su contenido.","okf_concept":"contracts/attestation-gate.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Gate de atestacion de reportes locales (.agents/logs, Nivel local)"}},{"id":"contracts/attestation-gate.md#104","metadata":{"content":"` siempre se excluye, sin importar su contenido.\n\n## Examples\n- Un REPORT sin envelope (texto plano, formato pre-gate) -> WARNING\n  `ENVELOPE_MISSING`, exit 0 en `main` (no bloquea reportes viejos).\n- Un envelope con `output_sha256` que no coincide con el hash real del\n  body pegado -> ERROR `OUTPUT_HASH_MISMATCH` (alguien edito el output\n  pegado despues de sellar, o el sello esta mal).\n- Un envelope completo y coherente (todas las claves, ambos hashes\n  calzan, `exit_code: 0`) -> `[]`, exit 0.\n- `task: otra-cosa` en un archivo `hello-world-REPORT.md` -> ERROR\n  `TASK_MISMATCH`.","okf_concept":"contracts/attestation-gate.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Gate de atestacion de reportes locales (.agents/logs, Nivel local)"}},{"id":"contracts/attestation-gate.md#105","metadata":{"content":"llo-world-REPORT.md` -> ERROR\n  `TASK_MISMATCH`.\n\n## Do / Don't\n- DO: recomputar AMBOS hashes (output y contrato) con la misma\n  normalizacion LF que `validate_contracts.py --hash` usa para\n  `tests_sha256` — coherencia de convencion en todo el repo.\n- DO: tratar `ENVELOPE_MISSING` como WARNING, no ERROR — reportes escritos\n  antes de este gate no deben romper retroactivamente.\n- DON'T: intentar verificar `agent`/`model`/`timestamp`/`repo_head` mas\n  alla de su presencia — son atestacion (afirmacion), no verificables\n  mecanicamente por este gate.\n- DON'T: agregar este gate a `.github/workflows/validate.yml` — la\n  evidencia que audita es local y gitignorada, un runner de CI nunca la\n  ve.","okf_concept":"contracts/attestation-gate.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Gate de atestacion de reportes locales (.agents/logs, Nivel local)"}},{"id":"contracts/attestation-gate.md#106","metadata":{"content":"al y gitignorada, un runner de CI nunca la\n  ve.\n\n## Tests\n(Los tests estan en `tests/test_validate_attestation.py`, oraculo\ncongelado con fixtures propios via `tempfile.mkdtemp()`.)\n\n## Constraints\n- Sin red, sin subprocess, sin LLM (`forbids`).\n- Solo stdlib (`deps_allowed: []`): `hashlib`, `os`, `re`, `sys`.\n- `touch_only`: unicamente `scripts/validate_attestation.py`.\n- No es paso de CI (ver seccion dedicada arriba); es herramienta de\n  verificacion local del PM, mismo tratamiento que `validate_perimeter.py`.\n- PARAR y reportar si necesitas conectarte a la red.","okf_concept":"contracts/attestation-gate.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Gate de atestacion de reportes locales (.agents/logs, Nivel local)"}},{"id":"contracts/attestation-gate.md#107","metadata":{"content":"RAR y reportar si necesitas conectarte a la red.\n\n## Criterios de aceptacion\n- [ ] `python -m unittest tests/test_validate_attestation.py` sale en 0.\n- [ ] `python scripts/validate_attestation.py .agents/logs .` corrido\n      sobre el repo real no lanza excepcion (el directorio puede no\n      existir o estar vacio localmente; eso es valido, exit 0).","okf_concept":"contracts/attestation-gate.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Gate de atestacion de reportes locales (.agents/logs, Nivel local)"}},{"id":"contracts/attestation-gate.md#11","metadata":{"content":"e de atestacion (validate_attestation)","okf_concept":"contracts/attestation-gate.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Gate de atestacion de reportes locales (.agents/logs, Nivel local)"}},{"id":"contracts/attestation-gate.md#12","metadata":{"content":"de atestacion (validate_attestation)","okf_concept":"contracts/attestation-gate