":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#34","metadata":{"content":"minista.\"\"\"\n```","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#35","metadata":{"content":"inista.\"\"\"\n```","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#36","metadata":{"content":"nista.\"\"\"\n```","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#37","metadata":{"content":"ista.\"\"\"\n```","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#38","metadata":{"content":"sta.\"\"\"\n```","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#39","metadata":{"content":"ta.\"\"\"\n```","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#4","metadata":{"content":"n pura: sin IO, sin red, determinista.\"\"\"\n```","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#40","metadata":{"content":"a.\"\"\"\n```","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#41","metadata":{"content":".\"\"\"\n```","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#42","metadata":{"content":"\"\"\"\n```","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#43","metadata":{"content":"\"\"\n```","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#44","metadata":{"content":"\"\n```","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#45","metadata":{"content":"```","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#46","metadata":{"content":"```","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#47","metadata":{"content":"``","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#48","metadata":{"content":"`","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#49","metadata":{"content":"## Invariants\n- Familias soportadas: `required` (ausente/None/\"\" -> violacion), `type`\n  (number|string|dict; number excluye bool; solo si el valor esta presente), `bounds`\n  (gt/min/max/integer; solo sobre numbers), `enums` (igualdad de valor, `in`), `refs`\n  (el valor debe ser clave en `refs[collection]`), `keyed_bounds` y `keyed_enums` (el\n  tope/conjunto se busca en `refs[table][record[key]]`; se saltan si la clave no resuelve),\n  `matches` (propiedad de texto `{field, pattern}`; `re.search`, anclar con `^...$` para\n  match total; ausente/None y no-string se saltan — trabajo de `required`/`type`).\n- `each` ({collection, where?, rules}): cuantificacion sobre colecciones — el subset\n  interno v1 (required/type/enums/bounds/matches, misma semantica) se evalua sobre cada elemento\n  di","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#5","metadata":{"content":"pura: sin IO, sin red, determinista.\"\"\"\n```","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#50","metadata":{"content":"isma semantica) se evalua sobre cada elemento\n  dict de la lista `record[collection]`, filtrado por `where` {field, equals}; toda\n  violacion lleva el prefijo del nombre de la coleccion (el campo top-level ES la\n  coleccion); coleccion ausente o no-lista se salta; elemento no-dict = violacion de la\n  coleccion nombrando el indice.\n- Campos punteados (`beneficiary.account`) navegan dicts anidados; un intermedio no-dict se\n  trata como ausente.\n- Orden estable de violaciones (por campo); nunca lanza ante record/ruleset con tipos\n  arbitrarios; una violacion por campo-familia como maximo.\n- El motor NO conoce el dominio de pagos: solo interpreta el rule-set.","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#51","metadata":{"content":"el dominio de pagos: solo interpreta el rule-set. La clave `code_only`\n  del rule-set no la evalua el motor (es documentacion de la frontera).\n- Determinista, pura, stdlib; sin red; sin subprocess; mensajes ASCII.\n\n## Examples\n- `evaluate({\"required\":[{\"field\":\"a\"}]}, {}, {})` -> 1 violacion que nombra `a`.\n- `evaluate({\"type\":[{\"field\":\"n\",\"kind\":\"number\"}]}, {\"n\": True}, {})` -> viola `n`\n  (bool no es number).\n- `keyed_bounds` de `amount` con `country=\"AR\"` y monto sobre `limits.AR.max_amount` ->\n  viola `amount`; con `country` fuera de `limits` -> no dispara (lo cubre `refs`).","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#52","metadata":{"content":"era de `limits` -> no dispara (lo cubre `refs`).\n\n## Do / Don't\n- DO: navegacion de campos punteada; orden determinista; mensajes que nombren el campo.\n- DO: saltar keyed cuando la clave no resuelve (evita falsos positivos y crashes).\n- DON'T: red, subprocess, IO, dependencias fuera de stdlib; ejecutar `code_only`; importar\n  el validador de codigo de pagos (el motor es agnostico al dominio).\n- DON'T: tocar el oraculo, el rule-set de pagos, el golden ni el test de equivalencia.\n\n## Tests\n(Los tests estan en `tests/test_rule_engine.py`, autorados por el orquestador y congelados\npor `tests_sha256`: el implementador no los escribe ni los modifica. Prueban cada familia\npor separado + determinismo + robustez, con rulesets sinteticos, sin el dominio de pagos.)","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#53","metadata":{"content":"n rulesets sinteticos, sin el dominio de pagos.)\n\n## Constraints\n- PARAR y reportar si... una familia del oraculo exigiera red/subprocess o algo imposible\n  con stdlib puro, o si el oraculo congelado fuera internamente contradictorio.","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#6","metadata":{"content":"pura: sin IO, sin red, determinista.\"\"\"\n```","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#7","metadata":{"content":"ura: sin IO, sin red, determinista.\"\"\"\n```","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#8","metadata":{"content":"ra: sin IO, sin red, determinista.\"\"\"\n```","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-rules.md#9","metadata":{"content":"a: sin IO, sin red, determinista.\"\"\"\n```","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-rules.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Motor de reglas declarativo (rule contract)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-specs.md#0","metadata":{"content":"# Contract: validate-specs\n\n## Intent\nQue ningún contrato de ejecución nuevo llegue a CI sin criterios verificables por\nmáquina, perímetro declarado y condiciones de aborto explícitas. Hoy ese checklist\nes manual en `specs/TEMPLATE-CONTRACT.md`; este contrato lo convierte en check\ndeterminista que lo exige el validador, no la memoria del PM. Mismo movimiento que\n`validate-okf` y `validate_contracts`, a escala de `specs/`.","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-specs.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Validador de contratos de ejecución (specs)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-specs.md#1","metadata":{"content":"f` y `validate_contracts`, a escala de `specs/`.\n\n## Interface\n```python\ndef validate_specs(specs_dir: str) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Valida todos los CONTRACT-*.md bajo specs_dir. Devuelve lista de findings\n    [{'file': str, 'level': 'ERROR'|'WARNING', 'rule': str, 'msg': str}],\n    vacía si todos los contratos son conformes. No lanza ante specs inválidas\n    (reporta). TEMPLATE-*.md se ignora.\"\"\"\n```\nCLI: `python scripts/validate_specs.py <specs_dir>` — salida y resumen en el estilo\nde `scripts/validate_okf.py`; exit 0 sin ERRORs · 1 con ≥1 ERROR.","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-specs.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Validador de contratos de ejecución (specs)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-specs.md#10","metadata":{"content":"; exit 0 sin ERRORs · 1 con ≥1 ERROR.","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-specs.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Validador de contratos de ejecución (specs)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-specs.md#11","metadata":{"content":"exit 0 sin ERRORs · 1 con ≥1 ERROR.","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-specs.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Validador de contratos de ejecución (specs)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-specs.md#12","metadata":{"content":"exit 0 sin ERRORs · 1 con ≥1 ERROR.","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-specs.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Validador de contratos de ejecución (specs)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-specs.md#13","metadata":{"content":"xit 0 sin ERRORs · 1 con ≥1 ERROR.","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-specs.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Validador de contratos de ejecución (specs)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-specs.md#14","metadata":{"content":"it 0 sin ERRORs · 1 con ≥1 ERROR.","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-specs.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Validador de contratos de ejecución (specs)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-specs.md#15","metadata":{"content":"t 0 sin ERRORs · 1 con ≥1 ERROR.","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-specs.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Validador de contratos de ejecución (specs)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-specs.md#16","metadata":{"content":"0 sin ERRORs · 1 con ≥1 ERROR.","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-specs.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Validador de contratos de ejecución (specs)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-specs.md#17","metadata":{"content":"0 sin ERRORs · 1 con ≥1 ERROR.","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-specs.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Validador de contratos de ejecución (specs)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-specs.md#18","metadata":{"content":"sin ERRORs · 1 con ≥1 ERROR.","okf_concept":"contracts/validate-specs.md","okf_type":"Task Contract","title":"Validador de contratos de ejecución (specs)"}},{"id":"contracts/validate-specs